<%# Availability, shown rather than hidden.

  The inventory classifies every capability as available, conditional or beta, and a conditional feature needs
  a named prerequisite before a reader can use it. Rendering the state beside the name is what stops this site
  repeating the old one's six over-claims; an available feature needs no badge, so only the exceptions carry one.

  BOTH STATES ARE SET IN THE LYN RAMP, AND THE SIZE COMES OFF THE TYPE SCALE. These were a yellow pill and a
  violet pill at an arbitrary 11px off the type scale -- two hues from no ramp on this site, inside the <h1> of
  every detail page, which is the one place a stray colour is unmissable. Conditional is now the quiet state
  (hairline on mist, soft ink) and beta borrows the link accent, so the badge reads as part of the page rather
  than as a status chip lifted out of an admin screen.
%>
<% if state == :conditional %>
  <span class="rounded-full border border-lyn-line bg-lyn-mist px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-lyn-ink-soft">
    <%= t('marketing.state.conditional') %>
  </span>
<% elsif state == :beta %>
  <span class="rounded-full border border-lyn-royal/30 bg-lyn-paper px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-lyn-royal">
    <%= t('marketing.state.beta') %>
  </span>
<% end %>
